Preserve binary Secret Service values and their content type with pass.

Binary values use a versioned Base64 JSON envelope inside the GPG-encrypted
entry. A non-UTF-8 prefix distinguishes it from every legacy text password.
UTF-8 text/plain values keep the ordinary pass representation. GPG writes are
checked and atomically replaced; reads drain stdout while GPG is running.
Readers of binary entries must use this patched provider.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/mdellweg/pass_secret_service/issues/39

